.Dd September 3, 2026
.Dt NATS-TUI 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nats-tui
.Nd terminal front-end to nats, the NATS command-line tool
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl mouse
.Op Fl context Ar name
.Op Fl s Ar url
.Op Fl creds Ar file
.Op Fl timeout Ar duration
.Op Fl nats Ar path
.Nm
.Fl json | Fl tree
.Op Ar connection flags
.Nm
.Fl version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows the server a
.Xr nats 1
context points at as a tree: its JetStream streams with their consumers,
its key-value buckets, its object stores and the micro services answering
discovery.
Every change is turned into a plan of
.Nm nats
commands that is previewed and only run after confirmation; the server is
re-read afterwards.
Nothing is changed except through
.Nm nats
itself.
.Pp
Reading is done with the NATS client library over the same context, so the
screen and the commands see the same server; the live screens (subscribe,
watch, events) stream from it too.
Messages are published and requested through
.Ql nats pub
and
.Ql nats request ,
and their output is shown.
.Pp
The options are the connection flags of
.Nm nats
and are passed to every command it runs; without them the selected context
and the environment of
.Nm nats
apply.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl mouse
Enable mouse support: click a row to select it, click it again to open it,
the wheel scrolls; in editors a click focuses a field and a second click
edits or toggles it.
.Ic m
toggles it at runtime; hold shift to select text while it is on.
.It Fl json
Do not start the TUI: print the context, the connection, the JetStream
account, the streams with their consumers, the buckets, the object stores
with their objects and the services as one JSON document and exit.
.It Fl tree
Like
.Fl json ,
as an indented text listing.
.It Fl context Ar name
The
.Nm nats
context to use
.Pq default: the selected one, or Ev NATS_CONTEXT .
.It Fl s Ar url
Server URL(s), overriding the context
.Pq Nm nats Fl s .
.It Fl creds Ar file
Credentials file, overriding the context.
.It Fl timeout Ar duration
Time to wait on responses
.Pq default 5s .
.It Fl refresh Ar duration
Re-read the server every
.Ar duration
.Pq like 5s
on the main screen, the details and the tables;
.Ic ctrl+r
toggles it at runtime.
.It Fl nats Ar path
The
.Nm nats
binary to run
.Pq default: Nm nats No in Ev PATH .
.It Fl version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh MAIN SCREEN
.Bl -tag -width "right/left/space/*" -compact
.It Ic up/down j/k pgup/pgdn home/end
Move.
.It Ic right/left/space/*
Expand or collapse a stream or a section
.Pq Ic * : all .
.It Ic /
Filter by name, subject or description;
.Ic esc
clears.
.It Ic enter
Details of the entity; a service instance is also asked for its request
statistics.
.Ic J
shows its raw JSON.
.It Ic e
Edit the stream, consumer, bucket, object store or context.
.It Ic a
Add what the row holds: a consumer on a stream, a key on a bucket, a file on
an object store, a bucket or store on their section, a stream elsewhere.
.Ic A
adds a stream.
.It Ic d
Delete the stream, consumer, bucket or object store.
.It Ic P
Purge a stream: everything, one subject, up to a sequence, or all but the
last few.
.It Ic v
Messages of a stream, one page at a time;
.Ic [
and
.Ic ]
page,
.Ic g
jumps to a sequence,
.Ic f
keeps a subject,
.Ic d
deletes a message,
.Ic a
adds a consumer filtered on the subject shown.
On a bucket the keys, on an object store the objects.
.It Ic t
Subjects held in a stream with their message counts.
.It Ic n
Fetch the next messages of a pull consumer
.Pq Ql nats consumer next ,
acknowledged, negatively acknowledged, terminated or left alone.
.It Ic u
Pause or resume a consumer.
.It Ic K O
Keys of a bucket, objects of an object store: put, get, delete, history,
revert, watch.
Editing a key runs
.Ql nats kv update
with the revision the key was read at, so a write that happened in between
is refused.
.It Ic s
Subscribe live to a stream's subjects or to typed ones.
.It Ic p R
Publish a message; send a request and show the reply.
A message can be scheduled instead: once at a time, once after a delay,
every interval or on a six-field cron line, to be published to another
subject when the schedule fires.
The stream holding the subject must allow message schedules.
.It Ic w
Watch a bucket or an object store live.
.It Ic E
Events: JetStream advisories and metrics, server events.
.It Ic I
Account information.
.It Ic M Ic T Ic L
The menus, described under
.Sx MENUS :
monitoring, reports and the cluster commands.
.It Ic C
Contexts: list, use, select, add, edit, copy, delete, validate.
.It Ic S
Use another context; every command then carries
.Fl -context .
.It Ic b B
Backup a stream to a directory, or, on a row without a stream, every stream
of the account; restore a stream or an account backup.
.It Ic y
Copy a stream's configuration to a new stream, which needs subjects of its
own: two streams cannot share a subject.
On a consumer, copy the consumer.
.It Ic x
Seal a stream or an object store (irreversible).
.It Ic m
Toggle the mouse.
.It Ic r
Re-read the server.
The consumers of a stream and the objects of an object store are fetched
when the stream is expanded or the store opened, and kept across reloads.
.It Ic ctrl+r
Turn the automatic reload on or off: every 5 seconds, or the
.Fl refresh
interval.
.It Ic h ?
Key map, help.
.It Ic q
Quit.
.El
.Sh MENUS
.Ic M ,
.Ic T
and
.Ic L
open a menu in the manner of the Lotus 1-2-3 control panel: two rows above
the tree, the first holding the items of the level you are in and the second
the items of whichever one is highlighted, so the level below is read before
it is entered.
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width "enter / down" -compact
.It Ic \(<- \(->
Move along the level.
.It Ic letter
The letter picked out in each word chooses that item at once.
.It Ic enter \(or \(da
Open a group, or run a command.
.It Ic esc \(or \(ua
Leave one level; at the top, close the menu.
.It Ic M T L
The key that opened the menu closes it from anywhere.
.El
.Pp
So
.Ic M T
is
.Ql nats rtt
and
.Ic M S L
is
.Ql nats server list ,
typed as fast as the fingers go.
Nothing else reaches the tree while a menu is up, and
.Ic /
stays the filter.
The accelerator is the first letter of a word unless the item names another
one, which is how Connections and Cpu keep a letter each.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic M Pq Monitor
Report (connections, jetstream, accounts, health, cpu, mem, routes,
gateways, leafnodes, downgrade), Check, Server (list, info, ping, mappings,
account info), Account (info, connections, tls) and Rtt.
The server commands need a system account context; rtt and the account
commands work with any user.
Check begins with This, the
.Ql nats server check
of the selected stream, consumer or bucket, and goes on to jetstream,
connection, meta, server, request and credential, the last few behind a
small editor for their thresholds.
.It Ic T Pq Reports
Streams, Consumers and Account (the three reports), Find (stream find,
consumer find), Gaps, and on a service row Service (info, stats).
.It Ic L Pq Cluster
The commands for the selected stream or consumer first (Stepdown, Peer;
Reset, Unpin), then Balance (streams, consumers), Meta (the JetStream meta
group: stepdown, peer), Reload, Kick and Purge.
Each one is a plan, previewed and confirmed like the others.
.El
.Sh EDITORS
Fields are moved with
.Ic up/down
or
.Ic tab ;
.Ic enter
edits a text field in place
.Pq Ic enter No keeps, Ic esc No reverts ,
.Ic space
toggles a checkbox,
.Ic left/right
picks a choice,
.Ic ctrl+s
is OK.
Lists are comma-separated; metadata is written
.Dq key=value .
Limits are -1 for unlimited; sizes take k/m/g/t; durations are 30s, 5m,
2h, 1d, 1w, 1y and blank for none.
Only what changed is passed to
.Nm nats ,
which prints the difference it applied.
Settings fixed at creation (a stream's storage, a consumer's mode and
policies) are left alone and mentioned in a note.
.Sh LIVE SCREENS
New entries are followed unless you scroll back;
.Ic end
follows again,
.Ic /
filters by subject or body,
.Ic c
clears,
.Ic enter
opens an entry,
.Ic p
publishes to its subject and
.Ic esc
stops the subscription.
The last 5000 entries are kept.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nats 1 ,
.Xr nats-server 1 ,
.Xr nsc-tui 1
